id: E550
trigger_tool: clang|gcc|make
phase: compilation
error_signature: use of undeclared identifier 'MAXNAMLEN'|MAXNAMLEN.*undeclared
severity: 2
category: compat, headers, libc, portability
match_keywords: MAXNAMLEN, pathname, dirent, PATH_MAX, undeclared identifier
title: Old BSD MAXNAMLEN pathname array fails on OHOS and can overflow
root_cause: Legacy C allocates a full directory path in MAXNAMLEN (a filename-only BSD bound); OHOS dirent.h does not provide MAXNAMLEN and merely defining it as 255 also permits directory-plus-name buffer overflow.
affected_scope: Old BSD/POSIX C tools that form directory/filename paths in arrays sized with MAXNAMLEN on OHOS musl.
verification_cmd: grep -n 'MAXNAMLEN\|PATH_MAX\|strlen(dirname)' miscfuncs.c && make -j1
rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: bounded-full-path
rec_description: Use limits.h PATH_MAX for the entire path and check directory and entry lengths before strcpy/strcat; alternatively allocate exact length dynamically.
rec_command: Add #include <limits.h>; change pathname[MAXNAMLEN] to pathname[PATH_MAX]; bound both dirname and dirname + d_name before copying; rebuild and test a directory path longer than 255 characters.
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: source-patch
fallback_priority: 2
fallback_approach: dynamic-allocation
fallback_description: Allocate each full pathname using strlen(dirname) + strlen(d_name) + 2 and free on every loop path.
fallback_command: Allocate per-directory entry with exact bounds and test under ASan.
fallback_auto_fix: false
fallback_impl: source-patch
forbid_1_pattern: define MAXNAMLEN 255
forbid_1_reason: A directory prefix plus a legal 255-byte name needs more than 255 bytes.
forbid_1_consequence: Undetected stack or static-buffer overwrite during directory watching.
causes: []
caused_by: []
similar_to: [E032]
conflicts_with: []
prerequisite_of: []
